# Change Detection & Notifications

## Purpose

Accept subscription requests, poll Edupage on a schedule, and notify subscribers when their program's timetable changes. Notification unit: one `studyProgramId` + `YearWeek`.

## Cron (`TimingService.refreshTimetables`)

Every 15 min, per study program in timetable DB:
- **Skip** if zero subscribers
- Refetch **current + next** ISO week
- Cached + different → notify all subscribers → update cache
- No cache → store silently (no false "everything new" alert)

`.join()` per fetch — one upstream failure can abort remaining work in that run.

## Diff algorithm

`TimetableDifference(newEvents, removedEvents)` — **no modified category**.

Set difference via `TimetableEvent.equals()` (`@Data` = all fields incl. enriched names). Same `subjectid` with changed time/room → one removed + one added. Clients needing "rescheduled" UX must diff by id.

## Delivery (`MessagingService.sendMessage`)

FCM (if token + Firebase init) → else email → else silent no-op.

**FCM data keys:** `newTimetableEvents`, `removedTimetableEvents`, `timetableKey`, `timestamp`, `summary`. Title/body via `TimetableChangeSummaryFormatter` (≤3 detail lines, 180 char trim).

**Email:** HTML with all added/removed events (time, date, teachers, rooms).

## Subscriptions

- Key: `(email, fcmToken, studyProgramId)` via `findByEmailAndFcmToken`
- Duplicate subscribe → 409 (`MessagingSubscriptionAlreadyRegisteredException`)
- Unsubscribe idempotent; `lastNotifiedAt` on successful send only
- FCM `UNREGISTERED` logged; row kept

**Edge case:** subscriber on two programs sharing an event → duplicate alerts for one real change.
